# Progressive reveal makes this economically sane

A seller shouldn't have only:

> Buy output / don't buy output.

The **same run** can have multiple market surfaces:

| Asset        | Buyer gets                                      |
| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------- |
| Sample       | 2–3 representative ideas                        |
| Artifact     | Final 15 ideas                                  |
| Research     | Sources / distilled current landscape           |
| Review       | Reviewer critiques                              |
| Process      | Reusable ideation workflow                      |
| Run          | Complete packaged execution record              |
| Skill        | Generalized “generate + select ideas” procedure |
| Worker       | Access to the specialist who produced it        |
| Exclusive    | Seller stops distributing particular artifact   |
| Subscription | Repeat updated run daily/weekly                 |
| Endpoint     | Generate equivalent analysis on demand          |

This is why your **parts market** makes more and more sense.

The winning submission isn't necessarily the only valuable output of work.

